  "difficultyRamp": {
    "within": "Questions 1 to 4 count only one kind in a mixed scatter (2, then 3, then 4, then 5 of the target). Question 5 builds exactly 5 from a large tray. Question 6 taps every group of 5. Question 7 shows the numeral 4 and asks the child to tap the matching group. Question 8 orders 1 to 5. Question 9 is a short story: Sam only wants one kind. Question 10 chooses the last number in 1, 2, 3, 4, blank. No adding two groups. No bonds.",
    "versus": "Easy is tidy 1 to 5 with tap-count and early hints. Medium is scattered groups of the same object, counts 2 to 5. Hard adds extra objects to ignore, a numeral match, a full 1 to 5 sequence, and a large build-set. Still the same node: count sequence, numerals and one-to-one to 5."
